From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sprite: do not assign __dict__ in __cinit__

Cython 3.1 and later reject assigning to a cdef __dict__ slot:

  src_c/cython/pygame/_sprite.pyx:148:12: Illegal use of special attribute
  __dict__

The assignment is redundant. Declaring "cdef dict __dict__" gives the type a
dict slot, and Python creates the dict on first attribute access, so Sprite
instances still take arbitrary attributes without it. pygame 2.6.1 is the
latest release and still carries the line.

diff --git a/src_c/cython/pygame/_sprite.pyx b/src_c/cython/pygame/_sprite.pyx
--- a/src_c/cython/pygame/_sprite.pyx
+++ b/src_c/cython/pygame/_sprite.pyx
@@ -145,7 +145,6 @@ cdef class Sprite:
     cdef dict __dict__
 
     def __cinit__(self):
-        self.__dict__ = {}
         self.__g = set() # The groups the sprite is in
 
     def __init__(self, *groups):
